    "https://www.augusta.edu/hr/jobs/general-info.php": {
      "title": "Application Guidelines & Hiring Info",
      "description": "Application Guidelines & Hiring Info Skip to main content This website uses cookies. Privacy Notice Accept Back to Top Apply Giving myAugusta Resources for: Students Toggle Audience Resources Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Alumni Community Search Augusta.edu Menu Academics Costa Layman Health Fair continues to thrive with its services » Academics Home Colleges & Schools Programs of Study Degrees & Programs Course Catalog Course Schedule Program Pathways Academic Calendar Online Programs Accelerated Degree Programs Resources Advising Counseling Services Honors Program Learning & Academic Support Libraries Testing & Disability Services Writing Center Outside the Classroom Army ROTC Study Abroad Experiential Learning First Year Experience Center for Undergraduate Research Career Services Jags Live Well Admissions Incoming MCG student earns USG student leader award   » Admissions Home Visit Campus Request Information Apply to AU First-Year Freshmen Transfer Students Dual Enrollment Graduate Students Medical College of Georgia Dental College of Georgia Opportunities Degree & Programs Honors Program Program Pathways Military-Affiliated Students New Student & Family Transitions On-Campus Housing Financial Aid Student Financial Aid Net Price Calculator Scholarships Cost of Attendance Apply for Federal Aid Campus Life SCCS inspires future innovators through VICEROY Kids Coding Camp  » Campus Life Home Athletics Community Army ROTC Living-Learning Communities Military & Veteran Services Mentorship New Student & Family Transitions Jags 4 Jags Mentoring Program Campus Services Dining Services Roarstore Housing Student Health Parking & Transportation Jagcard Get Involved Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Campus Recreation Student Government Jaguar Production Crew Intramural Sports Research CURS’ Summer Scholars Program celebrates discovery at annual symposium » Research Home Opportunities Undergraduate Research Graduate & Postdoctoral\n                                                            Research Clinical Trials Core Laboratories Innovation\n                                                            Commercialization Initiatives Cancer Cardiovascular Immunology Neuroscience Aging Resources Centers & Institutes Ethics & Compliance Institutional Review Board Sponsored Programs Tools for Researchers About\n                                AU Checkups and conversations: Inside the President’s Summer Tour » About AU Jagwire News Leadership President Provost Administration Enrollment Student Affairs Faculty Senate We are AU! Our Mission Working at AU Traditions History Augusta, GA Resources MyAugusta Calendar of Events Brand Guidelines Portals Faculty Directory Search Augusta.edu Resources For Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Alumni & Friends Apply Giving MyAugusta Close Search Search Trending Search Terms D2L LMS Email Pounce Calendar Registrar Housing Academic Calendar Financial Aid Parking Library Human Resources Information Technology Jobs & Careers About About Augusta University Applicant Requirements & Employment Process Map & Directions Job Listings University Executive Careers Juvenile Justice Augusta University Human Resources Jobs & Careers Application Guidelines & Hiring Info Application Guidelines & Hiring Info Navigating the job application process should be straightforward. This page outlines\n                        everything you need to know about applying for positions at Augusta University, including\n                        how to get application assistance, what documents you will need to provide, and how\n                        our hiring and background verification processes work. Application Assistance is available Human Resources is located at 1499 Walton Way in Annex 1. Computers are available\n                        from 8 am until 4:30 pm for public use to search and apply to career opportunities\n                        within Augusta University. Limited assistance is available for resume building. If\n                        greater assistance is required,  Augusta University has partnered with several community\n                        organizations that have trained staff dedicated to job search and resume building.\n                        To contact a HR Talent Business Partner, please call 706-721-1523 . Contact Us AU Human Resources Annex 1, 1499 Walton Way (706) 721-9365 HR_Web@augusta.edu Staff Listing Credentials & Degree Verification Any required documentation listed on the position posting such as degrees, diplomas\n                        and/or official transcripts, license, or certifications must be provided to the Human\n                        Resources office when you pick up your offer letter. We will be unable to complete\n                        your on boarding until all necessary documentation is provided.  All documents must\n                        be originals, copies will not be accepted. All certifications and licenses must be\n                        current and not within a thirty day (30) expiration period. Augusta University will only accept AHA BLS certification. If your position requires\n                        a Basic Life Support Certification (BLS) and you do not currently have an AHA certification,\n                        or if the expiration date is within thirty (30) days of your scheduled start day to\n                        begin orientation, you may go to the American Heart Association website to complete the written portion of the course. After doing so, contact the Center\n                        for Nursing Education at 706-721-8150 and schedule a BLS Skills Check-Off test.  Fees\n                        may apply. If you have a degree, diploma/transcript that needs to be translated and/or evaluated\n                        for credential purposes, please refer to a credentialing service such as the CGFNS International (also known as the Commission on Graduates of Foreign Nursing Schools).  Only degrees\n                        from US accredited institutions are acceptable. References As part of your application, it is required to provide a minimum of three references.\n                           References are to be of those individuals that you have had or currently have a working\n                           relationship with.  One of the references should be your most current supervisor or\n                           if unemployed, the most recent supervisor.  References from friends or relatives are\n                           not permissible.  For each reference, be sure to include their name, direct contact\n                           phone number, and employer name, and their working relationship to you. The names\n                           you provide should be familiar with your work history, work ethic and can be easily\n                           contacted.  It is always a good idea to let the references know that you have applied\n                           to Augusta University / Augusta University Medical Center, to prevent any surprises\n                           of not knowing. Minimum salary information There may be a minimum salary or a salary range listed for each position on the vacancy\n                           list. Hiring salary offers will not be lower than the posted minimum rate for the\n                           position. Actual salary offers are dependent upon the candidate’s qualifications,\n                           existing Augusta University policies, and the availability of funds for that department.\n                           It is important to demonstrate, on the resume / application, how past experience and\n                           education aligns with the posted minimum requirements. Position Information - It is recommended that you maintain a record of the position(s) that you have applied\n                           for.  Once submitted, applications, resumes, work samples, etc... become a part of\n                           Human Resources files and may not be retrieved for the applicant or be available for\n                           future job postings.  We recommend that you keep a copy of any job listing that you\n                           are applying for. Position Updates - Once a position is removed from the job posting, applications are no longer accepted. If\n                           a hiring department wishes to interview you for a position, they will contact you\n                           directly. Please do not contact the hiring managers regarding the status of your application.\n                           If you are interviewed and not selected for a position, the hiring department may\n                           contact you, but this is a courtesy rather than a requirement. Response letters will\n                           be sent to all applicants, either via email or US mail, once a candidate has been\n                           chosen for the position. Employment Eligibility ALL employees must initiate the Federal Form I-9, U.S. Department of Justice, between\n                           the offer extended date and no later than their third day of employment. Employees\n                           are required to complete the upper portion of this form, in the presence of a representative\n                           from the Division of Human Resources. Proof of eligibility to work in the United States\n                           is required to satisfy the Federal I-9 document requirements. A list of acceptable\n                           documents is included as part of the I-9 form and can be obtained from the Augusta University Human\n                           Resources office.  In addition, the new hire's Social Security Card will be required\n                           for criminal background authorization and payroll document verification. E-Verify - Through participation in the Federal E-Verify program,  Augusta University electronically\n                           verifies the employment eligibility and Social Security Number validity of all new\n                           hires. E-Verify is an Internet based system operated by the Department of Homeland\n                           Security (DHS) in partnership with the Social Security Administration (SSA). The program\n                           allows participating employers to electronically verify the employment eligibility\n                           of new hires and the validity of their Social Security Numbers. Employment Offers Contingent Offers All offers are contingent on a successful and satisfactory on-boarding which includes,\n                           at a minimum, the following: A county, state and federal criminal history check covering a minimum of seven (7)\n                              years; Drug screening; A nationwide sex offender search; A social security number check using the Form I-9 and the Federal E-Verify system; An educational/academic credentials check validation; National criminal database search; References verifications; Sanctions base; OIG/GSA ELPS review for exclusion from Federal and State programs, e.g. Medicare and\n                              Medicaid; and Credit checks for positions where employees typically have access to financial instruments\n                              or resources, for example, currency, checks and purchasing cards. Testing Pre-employment testing may be required for select position titles. It is the responsibility\n                              of the applicant to be prepared to take any of the required tests requested by the\n                              department. If you are unable to take the required tests during the time frame, it\n                              is possible that you may not be considered for the position. The tests are administered\n                              at the Human Resources offices. The Application Process Applications from candidates that meet the minimum requirements for education and\n                              experience for the position that they applied for are forwarded to the hiring department. The hiring manager/department reviews applications. A representative from the hiring department contacts selected candidates for an interview. After all interviews have concluded, the hiring department provides Human Resources\n                              with the name(s) of the candidate(s) of interest and all supporting documentation. A member of the Human Resources Staff will extend an offer of employment to the final\n                              candidate. Response letters will be sent, via email or US mail to all applicants at the conclusion\n                              of the search. Augusta Awaits You Search open positions and apply to join Augusta University today. Learn about our\n                              vibrant campus community, competitive benefits, and career growth pathways. Find Your Career Augusta University 1120 15th Street, Augusta, GA 30912 Campus Maps Campus Contacts A-Z Directory Degrees & Programs Employment Accessibility Accreditation Campus Safety Compliance Hotline Human Trafficking Notice Privacy Notices Title IX / Sexual Misconduct Apply Now Give Now © 2026 Augusta University Augusta University Facebook Augusta University Twitter Augusta University LinkedIn Augusta University Youtube Augusta University Instagram"
    },
    "https://www.augusta.edu/hr/jobs/university.php": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at Augusta University Skip to main content This website uses cookies. Privacy Notice Accept Back to Top Apply Giving myAugusta Resources for: Students Toggle Audience Resources Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Alumni Community Search Augusta.edu Menu Academics Costa Layman Health Fair continues to thrive with its services » Academics Home Colleges & Schools Programs of Study Degrees & Programs Course Catalog Course Schedule Program Pathways Academic Calendar Online Programs Accelerated Degree Programs Resources Advising Counseling Services Honors Program Learning & Academic Support Libraries Testing & Disability Services Writing Center Outside the Classroom Army ROTC Study Abroad Experiential Learning First Year Experience Center for Undergraduate Research Career Services Jags Live Well Admissions Incoming MCG student earns USG student leader award   » Admissions Home Visit Campus Request Information Apply to AU First-Year Freshmen Transfer Students Dual Enrollment Graduate Students Medical College of Georgia Dental College of Georgia Opportunities Degree & Programs Honors Program Program Pathways Military-Affiliated Students New Student & Family Transitions On-Campus Housing Financial Aid Student Financial Aid Net Price Calculator Scholarships Cost of Attendance Apply for Federal Aid Campus Life SCCS inspires future innovators through VICEROY Kids Coding Camp  » Campus Life Home Athletics Community Army ROTC Living-Learning Communities Military & Veteran Services Mentorship New Student & Family Transitions Jags 4 Jags Mentoring Program Campus Services Dining Services Roarstore Housing Student Health Parking & Transportation Jagcard Get Involved Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Campus Recreation Student Government Jaguar Production Crew Intramural Sports Research CURS’ Summer Scholars Program celebrates discovery at annual symposium » Research Home Opportunities Undergraduate Research Graduate & Postdoctoral\n                                                            Research Clinical Trials Core Laboratories Innovation\n                                                            Commercialization Initiatives Cancer Cardiovascular Immunology Neuroscience Aging Resources Centers & Institutes Ethics & Compliance Institutional Review Board Sponsored Programs Tools for Researchers About\n                                AU Checkups and conversations: Inside the President’s Summer Tour » About AU Jagwire News Leadership President Provost Administration Enrollment Student Affairs Faculty Senate We are AU! Our Mission Working at AU Traditions History Augusta, GA Resources MyAugusta Calendar of Events Brand Guidelines Portals Faculty Directory Search Augusta.edu Resources For Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Alumni & Friends Apply Giving MyAugusta Close Search Search Trending Search Terms D2L LMS Email Pounce Calendar Registrar Housing Academic Calendar Financial Aid Parking Library Human Resources Information Technology Jobs & Careers About About Augusta University Applicant Requirements & Employment Process Map & Directions Job Listings University Executive Careers Juvenile Justice Augusta University Human Resources Jobs & Careers Careers at Augusta University Careers at Augusta University Our employees are our greatest contributors to the legacy of achievement and promise\n                        that is Augusta University. As part of a premier organization dedicated to excellence\n                        in education, research, and patient care, we embrace the opportunity and the responsibility\n                        to make a real difference in the world. Apply as an External Applicant Apply as an Internal Applicant What Our Employees Say \"I’m grateful for the development opportunities AU offers—specifically the tools,\n                           resources, and training that help me learn and grow.\" — Sherita Williams , Allied Health Sciences \"I love working at my alma mater and collaborating with others on projects to help\n                           share Augusta University's story and its impact on our community.\" — Chris Curry , Georgia Cancer Center \"Working on a college campus is absolutely energizing! I am grateful for the opportunity\n                           to make a positive impact on the student experience.\" — Rhonda Banks , Philanthropy & Alumni Engagement Contact Us AU Human Resources Annex 1, 1499 Walton Way (706) 721-9365 HR_Web@augusta.edu Staff Listing Augusta Awaits You A comprehensive research university with an academic medical center located in the\n                        storied city of Augusta, Georgia, Augusta University provides boundless opportunity\n                        for employees to further their passion for teaching, discovery, service, and clinical\n                        practice on four campuses in Augusta and branch campuses across the state. Augusta University seeks to recruit and retain top talent across all disciplines.\n                        With a workforce of more than 12,000 dedicated employees, every team member plays\n                        a vital role in our mission to shape leaders, provide exemplary patient care, drive\n                        groundbreaking research, and work collaboratively to solve global challenges. Opportunities range from full-time benefits-eligible positions to flexible temporary\n                        roles tailored to your professional goals. The AU Advantage & Impact We are proud to offer a workplace culture recognized for excellence, growth, and inclusion: Recognized Workplace: Ranked by Forbes as one of America's Best-in-State Employers for three consecutive years and named the #2 employer in the CSRA. Inclusive Community: Ranked the #17 Most Diverse College in Georgia. Top-Tier Research: Designated a Carnegie Institution for Doctoral & Professional Universities. Comprehensive Benefits: Full-time university employees enjoy a robust total rewards package, professional\n                              development programs, tuition assistance, and competitive perks. ⚠️ Important Notices for Applicants Augusta University Human Resources will never contact you by phone or email requesting sensitive Personally Identifiable Information\n                           (PII), such as your Social Security Number or Date of Birth, prior to an official\n                           job offer. If you receive a suspicious inquiry, please do not respond and contact\n                           our HR department immediately. Device Compatibility Notice : We are currently resolving a technical compatibility issue affecting applicants on\n                           Apple devices (iOS/macOS). If you experience issues submitting your application, please\n                           complete your submission using a Windows PC or Android device with Google Chrome or\n                           Mozilla Firefox. We appreciate your patience while our team works on a permanent solution. Why Live and Work in Augusta? Education is big here. Quality of life is valued here. People are welcoming here.\n                           And your dollars go further here, with a cost of living well below the national average. The Garden City: Home of the world-renowned Masters Golf Tournament. Tech & Cyber Hub: Recognized as one of seven global cities destined to be a top cyber capital of the\n                                 world. Top-Ranked Suburbs: Nearby Evans, GA, was ranked the #1 Best Place to Live in America. Value & Excellence: Ranked the #2 Best Value College in Georgia. Need Assistance? Our Human Resources team is available to help you navigate the application process: In-Person Application Assistance: Visit HR at 1499 Walton Way (Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM) to access public computer terminals. Phone Support: Contact a Talent Business Partner at (706) 721-9365. Start Your Career Search open positions and apply to join Augusta University today. Learn about our\n                              vibrant campus community, competitive benefits, and career growth pathways. Apply as an External Applicant Apply as an Internal Applicant Augusta University 1120 15th Street, Augusta, GA 30912 Campus Maps Campus Contacts A-Z Directory Degrees & Programs Employment Accessibility Accreditation Campus Safety Compliance Hotline Human Trafficking Notice Privacy Notices Title IX / Sexual Misconduct Apply Now Give Now © 2026 Augusta University Augusta University Facebook Augusta University Twitter Augusta University LinkedIn Augusta University Youtube Augusta University Instagram ©"
    },
    "https://www.augusta.edu/hr/executive-search.php": {
      "title": "Executive Search",
      "description": "Executive Search Skip to main content This website uses cookies. Privacy Notice Accept Back to Top Apply Giving myAugusta Resources for: Students Toggle Audience Resources Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Alumni Community Search Augusta.edu Menu Academics Costa Layman Health Fair continues to thrive with its services » Academics Home Colleges & Schools Programs of Study Degrees & Programs Course Catalog Course Schedule Program Pathways Academic Calendar Online Programs Accelerated Degree Programs Resources Advising Counseling Services Honors Program Learning & Academic Support Libraries Testing & Disability Services Writing Center Outside the Classroom Army ROTC Study Abroad Experiential Learning First Year Experience Center for Undergraduate Research Career Services Jags Live Well Admissions Incoming MCG student earns USG student leader award   » Admissions Home Visit Campus Request Information Apply to AU First-Year Freshmen Transfer Students Dual Enrollment Graduate Students Medical College of Georgia Dental College of Georgia Opportunities Degree & Programs Honors Program Program Pathways Military-Affiliated Students New Student & Family Transitions On-Campus Housing Financial Aid Student Financial Aid Net Price Calculator Scholarships Cost of Attendance Apply for Federal Aid Campus Life SCCS inspires future innovators through VICEROY Kids Coding Camp  » Campus Life Home Athletics Community Army ROTC Living-Learning Communities Military & Veteran Services Mentorship New Student & Family Transitions Jags 4 Jags Mentoring Program Campus Services Dining Services Roarstore Housing Student Health Parking & Transportation Jagcard Get Involved Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Campus Recreation Student Government Jaguar Production Crew Intramural Sports Research CURS’ Summer Scholars Program celebrates discovery at annual symposium » Research Home Opportunities Undergraduate Research Graduate & Postdoctoral\n                                                            Research Clinical Trials Core Laboratories Innovation\n                                                            Commercialization Initiatives Cancer Cardiovascular Immunology Neuroscience Aging Resources Centers & Institutes Ethics & Compliance Institutional Review Board Sponsored Programs Tools for Researchers About\n                                AU Checkups and conversations: Inside the President’s Summer Tour » About AU Jagwire News Leadership President Provost Administration Enrollment Student Affairs Faculty Senate We are AU! Our Mission Working at AU Traditions History Augusta, GA Resources MyAugusta Calendar of Events Brand Guidelines Portals Faculty Directory Search Augusta.edu Resources For Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Alumni & Friends Apply Giving MyAugusta Close Search Search Trending Search Terms D2L LMS Email Pounce Calendar Registrar Housing Academic Calendar Financial Aid Parking Library Human Resources Information Technology Human Resources Contacts OneUSG Connect OneUSG Portal OneUSG Support Site Areas Benefits Campus Holidays Compensation Employee Relations Executive Search Faculty Support Services Information Systems Organizational Development Records Talent Acquisition Volunteer Services Jobs & Careers Service Recognition Augusta University Human Resources Executive Search Executive Search This is a truly exciting time to be joining Augusta University. Augusta University is headquartered in beautiful Augusta, Georgia. We also have campuses\n                        in various areas across the state including Albany, Athens, Macon, Rome and Savannah.\n                        We endeavor to provide each senior administrator with the foundation to be successful\n                        and productive. The Executive Search Team serves as a strategic partner in placing high-impact leaders who can drive organizational\n                           growth, transformation, and long-term success . About AU Office of the President Fast Facts of AU Mission, Vision and Values History of AU Contact Us AU Human Resources Annex 1, 1499 Walton Way (706) 721-9365 HR_Web@augusta.edu Staff Listing Executive Careers Our team is dedicated to delivering proactive and innovative search services that\n                        empower Augusta University to achieve its strategic goals. We recognize that exceptional\n                        leadership is essential to success and bring that commitment to every interaction—with\n                        executive stakeholders, community members, and prospective candidates. From initial\n                        vacancy to final recruitment, we work diligently to ensure a seamless and successful\n                        search process. Your success is our success. Current Executive Opportunities Department Chair, General Dentistry Associate Dean of Research – School of Computer & Cyber Sciences Vice President, Communications & Marketing Department Chair, Nursing Science Dean, College of Allied Health Science Dean, College of Nursing Nominate a Candidate for a Position Online Nomination form Attention Applicants Please note, Human Resources will never contact you by phone or email to request your Personally Identifiable Information\n                        (PII) such as your SSN or DOB. If you have questions or receive a suspicious request,\n                        please contact us. Resources Benefits The Augusta University offers a strong benefits package to employees. Learn more about\n                                       USG healthcare, retirement and well-being benefits offered by the university and the\n                                       University System of Georgia. Benefits Campus Maps Find where you need to go across all four of our campuses with our Campus Maps. Campus Maps Community Directory Augusta is a diverse and culturally vibrant city, filled with things to do, things\n                                          to see and, ultimately, things to know. Get started on your journey through the South’s\n                                          “Garden City” today! Community Directory Events Calendar To find out what events are happening on our campuses! Events Calendar Augusta University 1120 15th Street, Augusta, GA 30912 Campus Maps Campus Contacts A-Z Directory Degrees & Programs Employment Accessibility Accreditation Campus Safety Compliance Hotline Human Trafficking Notice Privacy Notices Title IX / Sexual Misconduct Apply Now Give Now © 2026 Augusta University Augusta University Facebook Augusta University Twitter Augusta University LinkedIn Augusta University Youtube Augusta University Instagram"
    },
    "https://www.augusta.edu/hr/jobs/juvenile-justice-health-services.php": {
      "title": "Juvenile Justice Health Services Careers",
      "description": "Juvenile Justice Health Services Careers Skip to main content This website uses cookies. Privacy Notice Accept Back to Top Apply Giving myAugusta Resources for: Students Toggle Audience Resources Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Alumni Community Search Augusta.edu Menu Academics Costa Layman Health Fair continues to thrive with its services » Academics Home Colleges & Schools Programs of Study Degrees & Programs Course Catalog Course Schedule Program Pathways Academic Calendar Online Programs Accelerated Degree Programs Resources Advising Counseling Services Honors Program Learning & Academic Support Libraries Testing & Disability Services Writing Center Outside the Classroom Army ROTC Study Abroad Experiential Learning First Year Experience Center for Undergraduate Research Career Services Jags Live Well Admissions Incoming MCG student earns USG student leader award   » Admissions Home Visit Campus Request Information Apply to AU First-Year Freshmen Transfer Students Dual Enrollment Graduate Students Medical College of Georgia Dental College of Georgia Opportunities Degree & Programs Honors Program Program Pathways Military-Affiliated Students New Student & Family Transitions On-Campus Housing Financial Aid Student Financial Aid Net Price Calculator Scholarships Cost of Attendance Apply for Federal Aid Campus Life SCCS inspires future innovators through VICEROY Kids Coding Camp  » Campus Life Home Athletics Community Army ROTC Living-Learning Communities Military & Veteran Services Mentorship New Student & Family Transitions Jags 4 Jags Mentoring Program Campus Services Dining Services Roarstore Housing Student Health Parking & Transportation Jagcard Get Involved Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Campus Recreation Student Government Jaguar Production Crew Intramural Sports Research CURS’ Summer Scholars Program celebrates discovery at annual symposium » Research Home Opportunities Undergraduate Research Graduate & Postdoctoral\n                                                            Research Clinical Trials Core Laboratories Innovation\n                                                            Commercialization Initiatives Cancer Cardiovascular Immunology Neuroscience Aging Resources Centers & Institutes Ethics & Compliance Institutional Review Board Sponsored Programs Tools for Researchers About\n                                AU Checkups and conversations: Inside the President’s Summer Tour » About AU Jagwire News Leadership President Provost Administration Enrollment Student Affairs Faculty Senate We are AU! Our Mission Working at AU Traditions History Augusta, GA Resources MyAugusta Calendar of Events Brand Guidelines Portals Faculty Directory Search Augusta.edu Resources For Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Alumni & Friends Apply Giving MyAugusta Close Search Search Trending Search Terms D2L LMS Email Pounce Calendar Registrar Housing Academic Calendar Financial Aid Parking Library Human Resources Information Technology Jobs & Careers About About Augusta University Applicant Requirements & Employment Process Map & Directions Job Listings University Executive Careers Juvenile Justice Augusta University Human Resources Jobs & Careers Juvenile Justice Health Services Careers Juvenile Justice Health Services Careers Join our dedicated team providing essential healthcare services within juvenile justice\n                        facilities across Georgia. Augusta University offers rewarding career opportunities\n                        for compassionate healthcare professionals and administrative staff looking to make\n                        a meaningful impact. How to Apply To view current openings specifically related to Juvenile Justice Health Services: Visit our job search portal using the link for External Applicants or Internal Applicants below. Enter DJJ in the search bar to display all Department of Juvenile Justice healthcare listings. Filter the results by city or location to find opportunities in your area. Apply as an External Applicant Apply as an Internal Applicant Career Opportunity Focus Areas We frequently recruit qualified candidates across a broad range of specialties, including: Clinical Care: Nursing, Physicians, Nurse Practitioners, and Physician Assistants Specialized & Behavioral Health: Mental Health and Dental Services Operations: Healthcare Management and Administrative Support ⚠️ Important Notices for Applicants Augusta University Human Resources will never contact you by phone or email requesting sensitive Personally Identifiable Information\n                           (PII), such as your Social Security Number or Date of Birth, prior to an official\n                           job offer. If you receive a suspicious inquiry, please do not respond and contact\n                           our HR department immediately. Device Compatibility Notice : We are currently resolving a technical compatibility issue affecting applicants on\n                           Apple devices (iOS/macOS). If you experience issues submitting your application, please\n                           complete your submission using a Windows PC or Android device with Google Chrome or\n                           Mozilla Firefox. We appreciate your patience while our team works on a permanent solution. Comprehensive Employee Benefits Health Insurance Dental Insurance Vision Insurance Life Insurance Supplemental Life Personal Accident Insurance Short-term Disability Long-term Disability Supplemental Health Insurance Retirement Tax Sheltered Annuity Deferred Compensation Dependent Care FSA Health Care FSA Health Savings Account Tuition Assistance Program Paid holidays Annual Leave Sick Leave Direct Deposit Augusta Awaits You Search open positions and apply to join Augusta University today. Learn about our\n                              vibrant campus community, competitive benefits, and career growth pathways. Apply as an External Applicant Apply as an Internal Applicant Augusta University 1120 15th Street, Augusta, GA 30912 Campus Maps Campus Contacts A-Z Directory Degrees & Programs Employment Accessibility Accreditation Campus Safety Compliance Hotline Human Trafficking Notice Privacy Notices Title IX / Sexual Misconduct Apply Now Give Now © 2026 Augusta University Augusta University Facebook Augusta University Twitter Augusta University LinkedIn Augusta University Youtube Augusta University Instagram ©"
    },
    "https://www.augusta.edu/jobs/external": {
      "title": "Augusta University Careers",
      "description": "Careers Skip to Main Content Press Control+M to start dragging object ptnbsid=5zAHLJNsPCBapISgBmYB9AddbLs%3d Back Augusta University Careers Menu Current search category:Menu Search keywords Press the Enter key to display the default suggestions, or input keywords to search. Search suggestions have been displayed. Use the arrow keys to review the results. Press the Enter key on a selected suggestion to navigate to that item. Search in... Menu Category All Company Directory Job Data No results to display Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Actions Search My Preferences Help Sign Out Augusta University Careers More Actions Augusta University Careers Sign In New User Welcome Sign In New User Thank you for your interest in employment with Augusta University. For your convenience, this applicant portal has been designed to allow you to easily access the complete list of available career opportunities using your desktop, laptop, or any mobile device. Within the portal you will be able to: View all career opportunities Narrow your search by using specific criteria to quickly locate jobs that interest you Create a search agent that will notify you when positions that match your search criteria are posted To submit your application, returning users will need to log in to your existing account. New users will need to create a new applicant account. For technical support or assistance completing a job application, please contact the USG Service Desk at (877) 251-2644 or support@usg.edu . For specific questions about positions at Augusta University, please contact the Augusta University Office of Human Resources at (706) 721-9365 and/or HRTalentAcquisition@augusta.edu . Due to an Oracle Known Issue, Mac OS users are advised to browse and apply for jobs using a web browser other than Safari. The Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and the Higher Education Act (HEA) fire safety provisions require institutions of higher education to publish an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report. These reports include crime and fire statistics for the three most recently completed calendar years, institutional policies and procedures for reporting crimes, and current policies concerning the security of, and access to, campus facilities and residences, as well as security considerations in the maintenance of campus facilities. The reports are available online at: https://www.augusta.edu/police/cleryandcrime/clery.php . If you would like to retain a copy of the report, you may print it from your browser or request a paper copy by emailing the institution at compliance@augusta.edu . View All Jobs My Job Notifications My Job Applications My Favorite Jobs My Saved Searches My Account Information"
    },
